  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, the greatest uncertainty is the absolute performance level of the simplest, most standard baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the most interpretable reference: it uses the primary modality in cellular profiling (RNA), the simplest profile setting, and a well-understood linear encoder (PCA-2000). Establishing this floor is essential before evaluating whether more complex choices (learned encoders, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, or multimodal fusion) actually add value. Without a clean baseline, any subsequent performance gain or loss is uninterpretable. This single experiment maximizes information per run by anchoring the entire search space and reducing uncertainty about the starting performance level, which is the prerequisite for every later comparison."
